and legend  states that whoever touches the Triforce  will have their deepest wishes granted  however the blessing comes with an omen  in that if an individual whose heart is  imbalanced touches the relic the  Triforce will split into its separate  pieces and seek out individuals who best  represent those pieces respectively it  cannot be known for sure why the  goddesses chose to leave behind such a  glorious and horrifying temptation  the races of the world to quarrel over  but the task of defending the relic was  given to the goddess hylia her  descendants and the sheikah tribe  now that we've refreshed our minds on  the purpose of the Triforce let's talk  about where it may be in the events of  breadth of the wild since breadth of the  wild has been confirmed to take place  after all three timelines let's retrace  our steps and figure out where the  golden relic was last seen in each of  the timelines starting with the child  timeline the Triforce is last seen in  Twilight Princess although never once  mentioned by name throughout the entire  game it is clear that the Triforce is  power exists within the three  individuals chosen of the goddesses link  zelda and Ganondorf differing from  several other Zelda titles in Twilight  Princess the three start off already  wielding the pieces of the relic within  themselves as displayed on the backs of  their hands at the end of the game when  link defeats the demon king Ganondorf  the Triforce of power refuses to empower  Ganondorf leading to his death we have  no evidence that the pieces leave any of  them following the final battle so it's  very possible that the Triforce pieces  continue to follow the descendants of  the chosen three through their  bloodlines in the adult timeline the  Triforce isn't mentioned in sphere  tracks or the Phantom Hourglass it is  however a pivotal plot device in the  previous game the Wind Waker in both  similarity but also in contrast to  Twilight Princess  the game begins in the same pattern with  the Triforce divided into its three  separate triangles following the events  of Ocarina of Time the Triforce of  wisdom rests with Zelda and power rests  with Ganondorf who has returned to  Hyrule  but the Triforce of courage was  shattered into eight pieces after the  hero of time left the adult timeline to  regain his lost days as a child  meaning the hero of winds does not  possess the relics power at the end of  the game the Triforce is fully assembled  again by Ganondorf  but King daftness wishes for the land of  Hyrule to be washed away forever after  granting the wish the Triforce  disassembles and disappears into the  distance implying its return to the  Sacred Realm after its use has been  depleted  since Hyrule was then washed away after  the events of Wind Waker this definitely  explains the triforces lack of presence  in the following games in the adult  timeline finally in the fallen timeline  the Triforce is shown in its entirety  all the way up until the last game  chronologically at the end of The  Adventure of Link it is reassembled and  used to reawaken the slumbering Princess  Zelda following these events we can  assume the Triforce follows the same  behavior pattern from the Wind Waker  meaning after it acknowledges and  completes a wish it returns to the  Sacred Realm where it rests indefinitely  we know where the Triforce is before the  events of breath of the wild but to  position it properly within the game we  still need to figure out which timeline  breath of the wild stems from as  mentioned before breath of the wild  takes place after all three timelines  but is not confirmed to take place in  any of them there are two theories I  think are each believable in their own  right the first is that it takes place  in the child timeline according to this  theory we know it can't take place in  the adult timeline because of specific  landmarks being present such as the  temple of time and Lon Lon ranch from  ocarina of time or the 